WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.164 --> 00:00:10.414
In tutorial 11.3, you'll
send your rankings, traffic,

00:00:10.464 --> 00:00:14.871
audits and AI figures to your own
warehouse, and chart them in Looker Studio.

00:00:15.901 --> 00:00:21.238
First, open Company settings, choose
Integrations, and scroll down to Data export.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:27.855
Click Add a destination. Storage
works with Amazon S3, Cloudflare R2,

00:00:27.905 --> 00:00:29.423
and other stores like them.

00:00:30.412 --> 00:00:34.537
Add your bucket, a folder, and
the access keys from your storage.

00:00:34.587 --> 00:00:36.574
Show me how explains where to find them.

00:00:37.933 --> 00:00:41.383
Or choose BigQuery. Add
your project and dataset,

00:00:41.433 --> 00:00:43.504
then paste the key file it gives you.

00:00:44.937 --> 00:00:50.122
Next, tick the tables you want: rank
history, your search figures, audit findings,

00:00:50.122 --> 00:00:53.367
AI visibility, backlinks,
and your analyses.

00:00:54.382 --> 00:01:00.502
For storage, also pick the file format:
a data file with one row a line, or CSV,

00:01:00.552 --> 00:01:02.516
which opens in any spreadsheet.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:07.540
Then choose how often: every day,
every week on the day you pick,

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:09.477
or only when you press Run now.

00:01:10.975 --> 00:01:16.695
Pick the time. It's in UTC, the world clock,
so choose one that suits your morning.

00:01:16.745 --> 00:01:21.459
Then click Check and connect. Alaventra
makes sure it can reach your data first.

00:01:22.453 --> 00:01:25.828
Your destination shows as
Working, with its schedule.

00:01:25.878 --> 00:01:28.412
Run now sends a fresh copy straight away.

00:01:29.453 --> 00:01:33.513
To change when it runs, click Schedule,
choose a new time, and save it.

00:01:35.932 --> 00:01:40.482
Every export is listed under Recent
exports, with how many rows it sent.

00:01:41.974 --> 00:01:47.836
Finally, to chart it all in Looker Studio,
create a read-only key under API access.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:52.515
Then click Show me how. The guide
walks you through adding the connector,

00:01:52.565 --> 00:01:53.988
one step at a time.

00:01:55.869 --> 00:01:59.794
Now your figures land in your own
warehouse, ready for your dashboards.

00:01:59.844 --> 00:02:03.228
Snowflake and Redshift can
read the storage files too.

00:02:04.223 --> 00:02:09.828
So, add a destination, choose the tables
and format, set a daily or weekly schedule,

00:02:09.878 --> 00:02:11.393
and connect Looker Studio.

00:02:12.412 --> 00:02:15.037
Your data now reaches your own dashboards.

00:02:15.087 --> 00:02:19.391
Next, connect an AI
assistant, in tutorial 11.4.
